  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-03-12T14:26:02.893Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When playing VRChat as streamer, i discovered one problem.... the mouth is not moving at all.\n\nI am sure there are streamers who want interact with chat channel BUT don't want get voice out in VRChat side (so users in VRChat don't hear your when you speak to chat viewers) you will turn mic off.\n\nBut the unlucky problem here, the mouth will not move and that is bit strange \"visual\" effect for viewers. They will see you with silenced face even you speak to viewers. \nOf course VRChat users can see you're speaking but there is no voice heard out.\nThis mouth movement option can added as well in the VRChat menu to turn it on/off if you want have mouth movement or not. \n\nIt's only to make stream more nicer for viewers with mouth movement. Some avatars with big mouth looks better if you're speaking to viewers as good visual effect. It's just strange if you keep mouth \"closed\" whole time while speaking to viewers.\nOnly voice part is turned off to not disturb others or let it out for others.",
